{
  "manufacturer": "Siemens",
  "manufacturer_slug": "siemens",
  "model": "SINAMICS G120 / G120C (Modbus RTU)",
  "model_slug": "sinamics-g120",
  "short_model": "SINAMICS G120",
  "aliases": [
    "G120C USS/MB",
    "CU230P-2 HVAC",
    "CU230P-2 BT",
    "CU240B-2",
    "CU240E-2",
    "CU240E-2 F",
    "CU250S-2",
    "G110M CU240M USS",
    "G120P"
  ],
  "equipment_type": "Variable frequency drive",
  "applies_to": "SINAMICS G120 with an RS485 Control Unit (CU230P-2 HVAC/BT, CU240B-2, CU240E-2 / -2 F, CU250S-2), G120C USS/MB and G110M CU240M USS, firmware V4.7, per Fieldbuses function manual A5E34229197B AA. Not SINAMICS G120X, which has its own documentation.",
  "summary": "Siemens' modular drive family (Control Unit plus Power Module) and its compact G120C variant. Control Units with an RS485 port run Modbus RTU as a slave when p2030 = 2. Holding registers 40100-40111 carry the PROFIdrive control word, main setpoint, status word and actual value; 40200-40522 map I/O, drive data, measurements, fault numbers and technology (PID) controller settings. This map covers that whole table except two registers: one with an inconsistent scaling entry and one with no stated bit polarity.",
  "transport": [
    "RTU"
  ],
  "defaults": {
    "unit_id": 1,
    "baud": 19200,
    "parity": "Even",
    "data_bits": 8,
    "stop_bits": 1,
    "tcp_port": null
  },
  "addressing": {
    "convention": "Modicon",
    "note": "Registers are printed as 40100-40522. The manual's request examples send 00 6D for register 40110 and 00 63 for 40100, so the wire address is the printed number minus 40001 (control word 40100 = address 99)."
  },
  "default_word_order": null,
  "firmware": "V4.7",
  "source": {
    "title": "SINAMICS G120, G120P, G120C, G120D, G110M Fieldbuses Function Manual",
    "doc_number": "A5E34229197B AA",
    "revision_date": "2014-04",
    "url": "https://cache.industry.siemens.com/dl/files/275/109981275/att_1314024/v1/A6V10556730.pdf",
    "pages": "Section 5.4 Modbus RTU pp. 94-104 (settings pp. 94-96, timing Table 5-10 p. 98, register ranges p. 98, mapping Table 5-11 pp. 99-100, FC03/FC06 and examples pp. 101-103, exception codes and p2040 pp. 103-104); RS485 Control Units Tables 5-1/5-2 pp. 79-80; STW1 p. 20, ZSW1 p. 21; fieldbus scaling 4000 hex Table A-1 p. 173, 047E hex example p. 174"
  },
  "notes": [
    "All values are single 16-bit registers. The table's 'scaling factor' is what the engineering value is multiplied by before transmission (e.g. 100 for 0.01 Hz), so the scale here is 1 / factor.",
    "Signed/unsigned is not printed per register; registers with a negative range are INT16, the rest UINT16. Ramp times (650.0 s x 100) exceed 32767 raw, which only fits as unsigned.",
    "Control and status word bits are the PROFIdrive STW1/ZSW1 layout ('all other telegrams' column of the PROFIdrive section), which assumes the default interconnection of the received/sent process data; they change if that interconnection is altered (e.g. free telegram configuration via p0922/p2079 = 999 or BICO changes).",
    "Left out: 40301 Converter firmware (scaling factor 0.0001 contradicts its printed range 0.00-327.67) and 40349 Control priority (HAND/AUTO text without a stated bit polarity).",
    "Table 5-11 labels 40401-40407 as 'Failure number, index 1..6' with index 2 printed twice; the parameter column (r0947[1]..r0947[7]) is used here.",
    "40001-40065 (MICROMASTER MM436 compatible range) is mentioned but not mapped in this manual, so it is not included.",
    "SINAMICS G120X is not covered by this manual; do not use this map for it without its own documentation."
  ],
